+### 4. External Patch Worker Mode (`aura_agent_arena_fireworks.py`)
 
-External agents can ask Aura to call a Fireworks model for a compressed micro-patch. This uses the user's Fireworks credits and stable prompt caching.
+The historical `fireworks-patch` command and MCP tool name remain for client compatibility, but the implementation is provider-neutral. Aura sends only compressed micro-context through the canonical egress router. Premium/code work starts with DeepSeek; fast work follows the cheap-provider order; every valid key is rotated; provider failure falls through automatically. Fireworks is now an optional late fallback.
 
-Environment variables:
-- `FIREWORKS_API_KEY` — required for Fireworks calls
-- `AURA_FIREWORKS_MODEL_FAST` — model for fast tier
-- `AURA_FIREWORKS_MODEL_CODE` — model for code tier
-- `AURA_FIREWORKS_MODEL_JUDGE` — model for judge tier
-- `AURA_FIREWORKS_SESSION_ID` — stable session affinity key
+Common secrets include:
+- `DEEPSEEK_API_KEY`, `DEEPSEEK_API_KEYS`, numbered DeepSeek backups;
+- `MISTRAL_API_KEY`, `MISTRAL_API_KEYS`;
+- `XAI_API_KEY` or `GROK_API_KEY`;
